// A #compiler call in deferred code (spec 6.12, 7.9) is refused once, at
// its name, though the statement is compiled again at each way out of its
// block: here three, two returns and the body's end. So is one in a defer
// that deferred code reaches, though each copy registers it anew. rig
// check, which never lowers the program, has nothing to say.
#import "Compiler";
main :: () {
    defer create_workspace("game");
    defer { defer create_workspace("game"); }
    if true { return; }
    if false { return; }
}
